            "pageCount": 2,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is an Adverse Event Report Form concerning a 54-year-old female patient with a history of hypertension and no known drug allergies. The report, submitted by her treating physician, Dr. Priya Nair from India, details a case involving the medication Neptazol, which the patient took at a dose of 20 mg orally once daily from July 1, 2026, to July 10, 2026. On the 8th day of treatment, the patient experienced severe facial swelling and a widespread rash, leading to a serious adverse reaction that required an emergency room visit and overnight hospitalization for observation.\n\nUpon admission, vital signs showed elevated heart rate and mild fever, but after 6 hours of observation, her blood pressure normalized, heart rate decreased, and temperature dropped. The outcome was positive, with symptoms resolving after discontinuation of Neptazol and treatment with antihistamines. Given the serious nature of the adverse event and the requirement for medical intervention, this document is highly relevant to patient safety review. It provides essential information on a significant side effect related to a specific medication, highlighting the need for further investigation into the safety profile of Neptazol.",
